<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedContent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a containment c and a schematic particular s if and only if s is the repeated content in c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An agent doesn't need to be a person, a living being or some other object that we would intuitively consider 'animated' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Host" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubPeriodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The year 1969 is a sub-period of the XX century, the period 1740-1751 is a sub-period of the period 1740-1789, the June of 1816 is a sub-period of the year 1816" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is the term of reference point or the reference framework for a movement, change, or comparison in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p enables an agent to affects some thing in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A living being that (i) is eukaryote - namely, has cells with a membrane-bound nucleus and organelles - and (ii) is heterothropic - that is, derives its nourishment from the consumption of other living beings" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Concretization enables schematic particulars to be located vicariously, by being located where their concretizations are; in general, a schematic particular is wholly present wherever one of its concretizations is present; since it can have multiple concretizations at the same time, a schematic particular can be located in multiple places at the same time" .
_:n79c81c57dfd0483097f8dc132c74bab9b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Objects are also typically material, but aggregates differ from objects because they are not unified by an internal organisation, function or form" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Repeated Content In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Here the word 'substance' is used in the chemical sense, and not in the metaphysical sense - which originated in ancient Greek philosophy and is still used in contemporary analytic metaphysics" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e' and an entity e if and only if e is a participant in e'" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Despite the similar local name, this class is much narrower than owl:Thing, which encompasses all entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is an instrument in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The possibility of absolute motion is controversial in theoretical physics and philosophy; however, this matter is operationally irrelevant, because in practice motion can only be assessed relative to a reference framework" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasReferencePoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eventuality that is either a parthood or a constitution" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In my arm being part of my body, my arm is the component and my arm is the composite; in a heap of sand having an individual grain as part, the heap is the composite and the grain is the component; in the composition of water by hydrogen, water is the composite and hydrogen is the component" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Regulations are the standard in a compliant business operation, best practices are the standard in a technical development, the workflow is the standard in the execution of a technical process" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointUnionOf> _:n79c81c57dfd0483097f8dc132c74bab9b1 .
