<https://loze-ontology.org/afterTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e occurs entirely after t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Loze Upper-Level Ontology" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Setting" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A containment with a repeated component is always going to have an associated number of occurrences (loze:hasNumberOfOccurrences)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing that is individuated by its position relative to other things - such as being enclosed by an object, being to the left side of an object, or being immediately North of another place" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a composition c and a particular p if and only if p is the composite in c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing that is individuated by a certain internal organisation, function, or form" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "It corresponds to owl:Thing" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A chunk of wood, a waterbody, the liquid contained in a tank, a heap of sand, the global petrol supply" .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Participant" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The distinction between concrete particulars and schematic particulars cuts across all the other divisions of the class :Particular: there are concrete objects and schematic objects, concrete eventualities and schematic eventualities, concrete aggregates and schematic aggregates, and so on" .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Composition" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubPeriodOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze.ttl with classes and relations for modelling living beings and social entities such as persons, groups, and organisations" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A particular entity that is not a way of being or a modification of other entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The destination does not need to be a place, but it can be a thing or a period of time too" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Object> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Affected In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/OrganisationOrgan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Group> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and an object o if and only if o is the setting in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Origin In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Groups don't include collections of persons who merely happen to have a common feature - such as the men, the persons with blonde hair, or the graduates - unless those persons also happen to be organised together or to interact with each other on a regular basis; such collections are best modelled as classes" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Waypoint In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Artefact> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Artefact can be either schematic or concrete: a software - in abstraction from its installated copies - is an artefact; a software's installed copies are also artefacts; a symphony - as a work of music, in abstraction from its performances - is also an artefact" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In other upper-level ontologies, relations like this are considered special cases of parthood, since the stages of an eventuality can be viewed as its 'temporal slices'; however, we prefer to suspend the judgment about whether the stages of an eventuality are to be considered among its parts" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eventuality that consists in one particular entity occupying a place partly or entirely" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasOrigin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Organisation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A company, a charity or foundation, a political party, a club, a state or government, an international organisation, a criminal gang, a terrorist organisation" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/OrganisationOrgan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The number of repetitions is going to be specified by the associated number of occurrences (loze:hasNumberOfOccurrences)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Intuitively, the participants in an eventuality can be viewed as the entities that are involved in it or play some role in it" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A simple, informal test for assessing whether an eventuality e is cause of another eventuality e' is to ask whether e'occurs (also) because of e, or whether the occurrence of e' is explained (among the other things) by the occurrence of e; if the answer is affirmative, then e entertains loze:isCauseOf with e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Repeated Content" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/LivingBeing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The precise definition of life and living being is controversial in philosophy of science and theoretical biology; still, the marks described in our definition are normally sufficient for assessing whether an object is a living being or not; nevertheless, there are still borderline cases, such as viruses and so-called super-organisms (e.g. coral colonies and bacterial biofilms)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Organisation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organisation" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Group" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAffected> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and an eventuality e' if and only if e' is a stage of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isStandardIn that obtains when the standard in question is an information artefact consisting of instructions for performing the eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Containment" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedContent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Instrument In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A book, an article, a physical document, a text or document file, a book chapter, a dish recipe" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Animal" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Constitution" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e' determines, modifies or qualifies e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Composite" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipe> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A red apple participates in its redness; Socrates participates in his wisdom; two spouses participate in their marriage; a killer, the victim, and the gun all participate in a killing; Italy, Austria and Germany all participates in Austria being located between Italy and Germany" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The construction of the foundations of a house is a stage of the construction of the whole house, the preparation of the dough is a stage in the making of a pizza, the positioning of the explosive is a stage in the demolition of a building, the fermentation of the must is a stage in the production of wine" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A carrot occupying the interior of a refrigerator, a sofa occupying a living room, an amount of liquid occupying the interior of a tank" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In my arm being part of my body, my arm is the component and my body is the composite; in a heap of sand having an individual grain as part, the heap is the composite and the grain is the component; in the composition of water by hydrogen, water is the composite and hydrogen is the component" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thing" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An intermediate stop in a travel, the ducts linking the supply point to a distribution point" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Dissectability consists in concretizations being iteratively divisible into parts of the same kind: a mass of water can be divided into other masses of water; a chunk of wood can be further divided into other chunks of wood; a piece of gold can be divided into smaller pieces of gold; and so on. Despite the appearence of infinite divisibility, we know from chemistry that this dissectability is going to stop at either the molecular or the atomic level: for example, a water molecule has no smaller parts that are themselves water, and an atom of gold has no smaller parts that are themselves gold" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "throughout Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred throughout the 1939-1945 period, the Thirty Years' War occurred throghout the 1618-1648 period, Napoleon's life occurred throughout the 1769-1821 period" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Repeated Component" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasConcretization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eventuality that consists in one particular being part of another particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parthood" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Text" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The core participants in a parthood are the part (loze:isComponentIn) and the composite (loze:isCompositeIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The house is the product in a construction work, the cake is the product in the context of baking, molecules are the products in a chemical synthesis, the zygote is the product in the fertilization of a female gamete from a male gamete" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/OrganisationOrgan> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A government's parliament, a company's committee, a team" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Product" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Stage" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a composition c and a particular p if and only if p is a component in c" .
