<https://loze-ontology.org/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a software system, a machine code might not be a text, because it's not always meant to convey meaning to humans; on the other hand, the source code is a text, since it's human-readable" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The victim is affected in a killing, the cake is affected in an eating, the car is affected in the repair, the house is affected in an alteration" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubPeriodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The gun is the instrument in a killing, the hammer is the instrument in the driving of a nail, the vehicle is the instrument in a journey, a debit or credit card is the instrument in a payment" .
