<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Only eventualities that have humans as agents (loze:isAgentIn) or are executed by objects designed by humans - like an automated system - can have a standard (loze:isStandardIn), since treating something as a rule or standard for an action requires human-like cognitive faculties" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "until Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/OrganisationOrgan> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The difference between an organisation organ and an organisation that is part of another organisation is that the official goals of an organ are entirely subordinated to those of the organisation of which it is part; by contrast, an organisation can maintain its own goals despite being part of a larger organisation" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
