<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Only objects can be settings, since they are the only particulars that have the sort of hierarchical structure in which something can occupy a role or function" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointUnionOf> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b7 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A particular entity that is a way of being or a modification of one or more other entities - qualifying them or making them be or go in a certain way - and is individuated by those entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHolder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e' and an entity e if and only if e is the holder in e'" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Determination Of" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and a composition c if and only if p has as component some other particular in the context of c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A product does not need to be a concrete particular, but it can also be a schematic particular: for example, a document or a book (in abstraction from its copies) is the product of a writing endeavour" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This relation does not apply to a person who is 'hosting' a party or to the 'host' of a game - who are rather agents in the respective eventualities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAffected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Content In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The arrival point in a travel, the distribution point in a utility supply, the buyer in a property conveyance" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The starting point in a journey, the supply point in a utility supply, the seller in a property conveyance, the seed in a plant growth" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasBeneficiary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Suggested Social Extension" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A room, the interior of a refrigerator, a tunnel, the left ventricle of your heart" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/fromTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred from 1939, the Thirty Years' War occurred from 1618, Napoleon's life occurred from 1769" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/LivingBeing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and a composition c if and only if p composes some other particular in the context of c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This thematic relation is intended for those eventualities that consist in roles, positions, or functions within a setting or an organised system; the participant that occupies the role is a theme in the eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a place occupation, the host is always a place, rather the object enclosing it - say, the interior of a refrigerator, rather than the refrigerator itself" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isInstructionIn that obtains when the instructions in question prescribes the ingredient ratio and/or doses and the procedure for producing concrete particulars of a certain type or with certain features" .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b10 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The concretizations of War and Peace are its copies, the concretizations of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 are its performances, the concretizations of Sachertorte are the individual Sachertorte, the concretizations of a software are its installed copies, the concretizations of the Toyota Corolla (as a car model) are its manufactured units" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The division between concrete particulars and schematic particulars cuts across the further sub-divisions of particulars: there are concrete objects and schematic objects, concrete eventualities and schematic eventualities, concrete aggregates and schematic aggregates, and so on" .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Plant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Plant" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A document (as opposed to its particular copies), a work of music (as opposed to its performances), an alphabetic character (as opposed to its inscriptions), a software (as opposed to its installed copies), a substance or material like water or gold (as opposed to their circumscribed portions), a car model (as opposed to its units)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "People with cancer are the beneficiaries in a donation to cancer research, a household is the beneficiaty in an allocation of subsidies for energy upgrades work to a company" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a constitution, the core participants are the composite (loze:isCompositeIn) and the schematic particular that is repeated in it (loze:isComponentIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "If x is a concretization of y and y is a determination of z, then x is also a concretization of z; one unit of the Toyota Corolla hatchback is also a unit of the Toyota Corolla; a heavy water molecule is a water molecule; and so on" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Schematic Particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAgent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze.ttl with relations for locating eventualities relative to periods of time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Topic" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze.ttl with classes and relations for modelling substances and material composition" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/afterTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The relation obtains even if the eventuality does not occur immediately after the period of time: for example, WWII occurred after 1900, even though it only started in 1939" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Person" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Object> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubPeriodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between two periods of time of which the former is a part or segment of the latter" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An eventuality is not general, but is linked to its participants - that is, the entities that bear it or are involved in it; the wisdom of Socrates is numerically distinct from the wisdom of Diogenes, and they existed at different times; the redness of this apple is distinct from the redness of that other apple, and so on" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/OrganisationOrgan> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A group that (i) is part of an organisation, (ii) it serves a specific function in the organisation in question, and (iii) it not itself an organisation" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The Toyota Corolla Hatchback is a determination of the Toyota Corolla; the 1869 version of War and Peace is a determination of War and Peace; Apocalypse Now Redux is a determination of Apocalypse Now; heavy water is a determination of water; anthracite is a determination of coal; carbon-14 is a determination of carbon" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasOrigin> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Stage Of" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Plant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A living being that (i) is eukaryote - namely, has cells with a membrane-bound nucleus and organelles - and (ii) derives its nourishment from photosynthesis" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In practice, the function of this class of eventualities is to describe the overall composition of a particular without giving an enumeration of its individual parts" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a containment, the core participants are the container (loze:isHostIn) and the content (loze:isContentIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Multiple eventualities can entertain the relation :isCauseOf with a given eventuality, since an eventuality can have more than one cause" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b9 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasNumberOfOccurrences> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e' and an entity e if and only if e is a topic in e'" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasNumberOfOccurrences> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This relation is mostly intended to be used in the context of compositions (loze:Composition) and containments (loze:Containment); that being said, its application to other eventualities should not be excluded in principle" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The house is the host in a residency or occupation, the tank is the host in the containment of a liquid, the duct is the host in the flow of a fluid, the place is the host in a position or location" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing that is individuated by its coordinates across the temporal axis" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of a cake having as ingredient 200 grams of wheat flour, wheat flour is the ingredient; in the case of a solution having as ingredient 2 litres of water, water is the ingredient" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e ends at t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An object persists over time as long as it preserves the internal organisation, function, or form that individuates it; as long as that is preserved, the parts of the objects and their types can change without causing the object to go out of existence" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Recipient" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The function of this relation is to specify the temporal location of an eventuality as a whole" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Object> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasBeneficiary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAffected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An arm being part of a person, a wall being part of a house, a compressor being part of a refrigerator, a wood board being part of a table, a nucleus being part of an atom, Mars being part of the solar system, the lithosphere being part of the Earth, a movement being part of symphony, hydrogen atom being part of water molecule" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Artefacts, Information, and Instructions" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e is a subject matter of cognition or meaning in the context of e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is brought into existence by some other particular in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a concrete particular c and a schematic particular s if and only if (1) c exemplifies or has the main features of s, and (2) s provides the benchmark or the norm for the properties and the behaviour of c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Particular entities are to be contrasted with classes; the concept of a particular mostly corresponds to the Semantic Web concept of an individual or instance" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasConcretization> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a thing t and an eventuality e if and only t is affected by a thing - the agent - in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/atTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII was happening at 1943, the French Revolution was happening at 1790, the Italian Renaissance was happening at 1513" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A human, a horse, a molecule, a table, a computer, a planet, a paracetamol tablet" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/afterTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Text> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Differently from Schematic particulars, a concrete particular only occupies one place or location at a time: my copy of War and Peace occupies one slot in my bookcase right now; I can only occupy one place at a time; a unit of Toyota Corolla is in one place at a time; a particular performance of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 takes place in one and only one venue" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An eventuality in which a particular is positioned within and physically constrained by another object" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/fromTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Standard In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Substance repetition is impractical to account for in terms of number of occurrences, since the units are too many to be counted; consequently, instead of using loze:hasNumberOfOccurrences, it is advisable to specify quantities based on units of measure" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Product In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A box containing eggs, a glass containing a portion of water, a dwelling containing pieces of furniture" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Repeated Component In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Composite In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is in a certain state or occupies a position in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An eventuality can have an agent without having patients or products: for example, Joe's walking has Joe has agent, but no patient or product" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The payee is the recipient in a payment, the buyer is the recipient in a property conveyance, the addressee is the recipient in a shipping, the donee is the recipient in a donation" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/fromTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Organisation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An organisation can have other organisations as parts: for example, a company can have other companies - its subsidiaries - as parts" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "While the repeated content is always going to be a schematic particular, the host can be either a schematic particular or a concrete particular" .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Place> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
