<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Recipe" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Held" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a thing t and an eventuality e if and only if t acts or causes changes in some thing in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b11 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An artefact that consists of a structured system of symbols' occurrences meant to convey information" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/LivingBeing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/LivingBeing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An object that displays properties such as responsiveness, growth, metabolism, energy transformation, and reproduction" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In some cases, the beneficiary of an eventuality is the same as the patient: for example, the beneficiary of successful a medication, therapy, or surgical operation is the patient" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of a monomer making up a polymerous sequence, the monomer is the repeated component; in the case of water having two atoms of hydrogen, hydrogen atom is the repeated component; in the case of an engine having pistons of a certain type, the piston - construed as a schematic object - is the repeated component" .
_:n79c81c57dfd0483097f8dc132c74bab9b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Person> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The scope of this thematic relation is not limited to motion, but also encompasses other types of changes as well as comparisons: for example, if an eventuality consists in an object being larger than another one, the larger object will be the theme and the other will be the reference point" .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Content" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Holder In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information artefact that consists of sentences in some human-readable language and is meant to convey meaning to humans" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a composition c and a schematic particular s if and only if s is the repeated component in c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a product in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e' and an entity e if and only if e is held in e'" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/beforeTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred before 1960, the birth of Napoleon occurred before 1800" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStandard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/LivingBeing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Living Being" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An entity that is not a class or type of entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A particular that is bounded to one spatial location at a time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Instruction In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasIngredient> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Theme In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains betwen an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e occurs throughout a a sub-period of t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/NonHumanAnimal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an object o and an eventuality e if and only if o is the setting or context in which e is the case" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Artefact> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Concrete Particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Animals typically have a more flexible body than plants and fungi and are able to move" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred until 1945, the Thirty Years' War occurred until 1648, Napoleon's life occurred until 1821" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Recipe In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubPeriodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between two eventualities e and e' if and only if e is a stage or phase in the occurrence of e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Topic In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasNumberOfOccurrences> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Number Of Occurrences" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e controls or is super-ordinated to some other entity in the context of e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/NonHumanAnimal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAffected> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a thing t if and only if t is affected in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasReferencePoint> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the person or organisation is the holder in a possession or ownership; the manager is the holder in a management relationship with the managed employee" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Plant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Within biological taxonomy - so-called Tree of Life - plants are the members of the kingdom of Plantae" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Copper, gold, water, wood, kerosene, steel, wheat flour, sugar, liquid acrylic paint" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/atTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This relation doesn't necessarily relate an eventuality to the entire period of time when it occurs; for example, WWII started in 1939 and ended in 1945, but it was still in course in 1943, so it entertains the relation loze:atTime with 1943 too" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/fromTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "from Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The concretizations of a schematic particular can deviate from it in various respects: for example, most performances of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 typically lasts between 65 and 75 minutes, but the 2018 performance from the Philarmonia Orchestra conducted by Benjamin Zander only lasts 58 minutes; in some cases, the deviation is merely an anomaly, but in other cases it entails that the concretization is defective, faulty, or bad, like a poorly made Sachertorte, or a faulty Toyota Corolla unit" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of a blister pack containing 10 standardised 5 mg paracetamol tablets, the 5 mg paracetamol tablet - construed as a schematic particular - is the repeated content" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Artefact> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An object that is designed and made by humans for serving certain purposes or functions" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/afterTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "after Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Your arm, one Toyota Corolla unit, the computer in front of you, the portion of water in a given glass, a piece of gold, one performance of Beethoven's Symphony No 9, the stabbing of Caesar from Brutus, a heap of sand, your bedroom, the last hour" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Ingredient In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "It does not encompass those entities that in the legal jargon are called 'legal persons' or 'non-physical persons' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Person> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A polymerous sequence being made up by repetitions of a given monomer; an aggregate of tablets being made up by one tablet (construed as a schematic object) repeated in 10 occurrences" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The change in question does not need to be a movement, but it can be a qualitative or quantitative change too: for example, if an eventuality consists in one object becoming more similar to another one, the latter will be the destination" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Given an eventuality e and a period of time t, e can have at the most one stage that occurs from the start to the end of t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasNumberOfOccurrences> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that assignes to an eventuality the number of occurrences in which a certain schematic particular is repeated in the context of that eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The information carried by an information artefact does not need to be intelligible for humans: for example, certain files or codes carry informaton that is only meant to be executed by a machine" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p encloses, accommodates or contains some other particular in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Two period of time can have exactly the same duration and yet be distinct period of time, because they have distinct beginnings and ends; for example, this hour and the next hour are two distinct periods, despite having the exact same duration of 60 minutes" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasReferencePoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/atTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e is the case or is occurring at t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The assembly manual is the instruction in the assembly of a piece of furniture, the cookbook recipe is the instruction in the preparation of a cake, the workflow documentation is the instruction in the execution of a technical process, a computer programme or software is the instruction in a computational process or programme execution" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasNumberOfOccurrences> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In a composition in which a polymerous sequence has a monomer repeated 3000 times, the number of occurrences is 3000; in the composition of the water molecule out of hydrogen, the number of occurrences is 2; in a containment in which a tablet is repeated 10 times in a blister pack, the number of occurrences is 10" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/fromTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e starts occurring at t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only p is enclosed or contained by some other particular in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Every eventuality that has an affected thing also has some agent" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze.ttl with classes and predicates related to artefacts, information artefacts, and instructions" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Beneficiary In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The cookbook doses and instructions are the recipe in the preparation of a cake, a pharmaceutical formulation is the recipe in the production of paracetamol tablets, the alloy formula togethet with the alloying instructions are the recipe in the manufacturing of steel slabs" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Compared to an affected thing, the recipient is impacted or controlled less directly in the context of the eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointUnionOf> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b5 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A given thing can be both agent and patient in the same eventuality: for example, a person washing themselves is both agent and patient in a washing; in a handshake greeting, both persons are both agents (since they are shaking the other person's hand) and patient (since their own hand is being shaken)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An object that consists of persons that are associated to each other by some socially significant relation or recurrent interaction" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An animal that is a specimen of the species Homo sapiens" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Animal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Within biological taxonomy - so-called Tree of Life - animals are the members of the kingdom of Animalia" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Plant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Plants typically have a firmer cellular structure than animals and are not able to move" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An schematic particular has the force of a determinant with regard to its concretizations: the structure of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 dictates the structure of its performances; the specifications of the Toyota Corolla are the benchmark for the features of its units; the chemical properties of water determine the behaviour of concrete portions of water" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Differently from classes, schematic particulars share their main features with their instances; for example, a book has chapters just like its copies, a piece of music has the same harmonic structure as its performances, an alphabetic character has the same shape as its inscriptions, a car model has similar features as its units" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Determination" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHolder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Every eventuality that has a product also has some agent" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
_:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b6 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p benefits from what happens in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the host in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Cause" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Standard" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Temporal Relations" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/atTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "at Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Similarly to classes, schematic particulars are not bounded to one particular location at a time: as a rule, a schematic particular is wholly present wherever one of its concretizations is present; War and Peace is present wherever one of its copies is present; water is present wherever one or more H2O molecules are present; the Toyota Corolla is present wherever one of its units is present" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Participant In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In formal mereology, one particular being 'entirely made up' by repeated occurrences, means that it is identical to the mereological sum of those occurrences: as an approximation, this means that its only parts are those occurrences and the parts of those occurrences; more rigorous definitions can be found in the philosophical literature on formal mereology" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "There is an obvious sense in which even objects can host other particulars: for example, a house can host people and artefacts; likewise, a tank can host amounts of liquid; however, places host things by being occupied by them, whereas objects host things by having them within themselves - that is, by having them occupying the place that they enclose" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasReferencePoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the reference point in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointUnionOf> _:n063a40871ee841d298f54ea38223eb81b1 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aggregate" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "within Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Informally, determination consists in the gradual increase in detailing and specificity of a schematic particular; it can be viewed as the schematic particulars' counterpart of subclasshood" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Theme" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasOrigin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the origin in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The origin does not need to be a place, but it can be a thing or a period of time too" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasBeneficiary> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An aggregate can also be scattered across space - such as the total water reserve of England or the amount of methane used for heating my house over the last year - in which case its individuation is based on a combination of material composition and practical interests" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Reference Point In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/beforeTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The possessed thing is the held in a possession or ownership; the managed employee is the held in a management relationship" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "WWII occurred within the XX century, the Thirty Years' War occurred within the 1620-1650 period, the Italian Renaissance occurred within the second millenium" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing that is individuated by some stable material composition or spatial contiguity" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/atTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Joe is the topic in an identity check, an electrical system is the topic of an electrical safety report, cancer (as a schematic particular or a class of eventualities) is the topic in a cancer research, liberty is the topic of John Stuart Mill's essay 'On Liberty', a book (in abstraction from its copies) is the topic of a review" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isComponentIn that obtains whenever the component is a substance that occurres in the composite in a given amount" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRepeatedContent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This is intended as a broad, comprehensive category that encompasses the entities that in other ontologies and category systems are variously called 'qualities', 'attributes', 'relations, 'events', 'processes', 'facts', 'specifically dependent continuants' etc..." .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entity" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasIngredient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Ingredient" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "While the repeated component is always going to be a schematic particular, the composite can be either a schematic particular or a concrete particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
